prompt:
Read all canonical Stock Research Lab documents and prior audit/experiment
results before working.

Review especially:

- docs/historical-research-protocol.md
- docs/top30-observation-contract.md
- docs/audits/JOB-0006-point-in-time-leakage-audit.md
- docs/audits/JOB-0009-legacy-historical-artifact-audit.md
- docs/experiments/JOB-0010-telegram-provenance-repair.md
- src/research_contracts/top30.py
- src/research_contracts/historical_fixture.py
- existing Telegram parser-related legacy code

TARGET REPOSITORY

D:/Project/research

LEGACY CODE REFERENCE

D:/Project/stock-trading-system-reference

Treat as strictly READ ONLY.

LEGACY DATA REFERENCE

D:/Project/stock

Treat as strictly READ ONLY.

TARGET REAL SOURCE

Telegram message ID: 15617

Legacy raw artifact:

D:/Project/stock/data/telegram/daily/2023-09-01_07-36-30_15617.txt

JOB-0010 provenance-repair evidence and restricted fixture manifest must be
treated as the authoritative provenance inputs for this experiment.

IMPORTANT EXISTING CLASSIFICATION

JOB-0010 classified this artifact as:

B_SOURCE_VERIFIED_CONTENT_STRONGLY_SUPPORTED

The current Telegram content canonically matches the preserved legacy
artifact, but exact historical cutoff-visible byte availability is NOT fully
proven.

Therefore availability remains insufficient for historical assessment.

OBJECTIVE

Build the minimum real-source parsing path:

genuine restricted Telegram artifact
    ->
verified fixture/provenance
    ->
parser
    ->
PreAssessmentTop30 representation
    ->
QUARANTINE

The output must preserve source-observed information while preventing it from
becoming a historical Top30Observation, AssessmentPayload, or frozen
assessment while availability remains insufficient.

This job is NOT an outcome experiment.

Do not access future price data.

Do not broaden to other Telegram messages.

Do not process the full three-year dataset.

PART 1 — LEGACY PARSER REVIEW

Inspect the minimum relevant legacy parser implementation.

Determine:

- how a Top30 Telegram report is recognized;
- how report date/time is extracted;
- how stock rows are extracted;
- how rank/order is represented;
- how stock names are preserved or normalized;
- how returns/percent fields are parsed if present;
- how malformed rows are handled;
- where manual corrections historically entered the pipeline.

Do not migrate the full parser architecture.

Reuse or adapt only the minimum parsing logic needed for this real artifact.

PART 2 — PRE-ASSESSMENT CONTRACT

Introduce a small explicit pre-assessment representation if one does not
already exist.

It must represent parsed source observations that are genuine but not yet
eligible for historical assessment.

Preserve at minimum:

- source artifact/provenance reference;
- Telegram message ID;
- source timestamp;
- report/cutoff candidate;
- exact source-observed stock name;
- rank/order when available;
- source-observed numeric fields when safely parseable;
- parser version;
- provenance/evidence classification;
- availability state;
- quarantine reason;
- unresolved identity state where applicable.

The representation must NOT imply historical assessment eligibility.

PART 3 — EXACT SOURCE NAME PRESERVATION

Preserve the exact stock name observed in the genuine Telegram source.

If the legacy parser historically normalized names:

- retain raw/source name separately;
- normalization may be represented as parser output metadata;
- never replace source-observed identity silently.

Do not use current KRX/master mapping to fill codes.

PART 4 — CORRECTION BOUNDARY

Check message 15617 against the authoritative correction registry:

D:/Project/stock/data/manual/telegram/top30_corrections.csv

JOB-0010 found zero corrections for this message.

Verify this remains true.

Do not apply corrections from unrelated messages.

The parser architecture must keep future correction/enrichment layers separate
from immutable raw source observations.

PART 5 — QUARANTINE GATE

Implement an explicit gate between pre-assessment parsing and
Top30Observation/AssessmentPayload.

Because JOB-0010 availability is not cutoff-verified, message 15617 must NOT
be promoted into assessment-time data.

Attempts to promote it must fail explicitly.

Do not rely on developer convention or documentation alone.

Enforce this in code.

A restricted real source may be parsed and inspected, but must remain
quarantined until a later research-policy decision explicitly permits its
evidence class.

PART 6 — FORBIDDEN OUTPUTS

For this message, while availability remains insufficient, the pipeline must
not produce:

- assessment-eligible Top30Observation;
- AssessmentPayload;
- frozen assessment;
- historical resolved identity based on current master;
- future/outcome labels.

If existing APIs allow one of these paths, treat it as a leakage/integrity bug
and fix it locally with regression tests.

PART 7 — PARSING RESULT

Parse exactly message 15617.

Report:

- whether it is recognized as a Top30 report;
- parsed report timestamp/date;
- row count;
- rank/order coverage;
- exact source names;
- malformed/skipped row count;
- duplicate row behavior;
- source numeric fields parsed;
- unresolved identity count;
- quarantine reason.

Do not manually alter the source to achieve 30 rows.

If parser output differs from expected source content, investigate and report
the reason.

PART 8 — DETERMINISM

Parsing the same immutable source artifact with the same parser version must
produce deterministic pre-assessment output.

Create a digest for the deterministic parsed representation.

Bind it to:

- source fixture digest;
- provenance repair record;
- parser version;
- parsed representation digest.

A source byte change or parser-version change must be detectable.

PART 9 — MACHINE-READABLE ARTIFACT

Create a small deterministic pre-assessment artifact under the target research
data structure.

It must clearly identify itself as:

QUARANTINED / NOT ASSESSMENT ELIGIBLE

Do not name or structure it in a way that could be confused with a frozen
assessment.

PART 10 — TESTS

Add focused tests proving at minimum:

1. genuine fixture digest is validated before parsing;
2. source byte mismatch blocks parsing;
3. parser recognizes the real message format;
4. exact source stock names are preserved;
5. row ordering/rank is deterministic;
6. malformed rows cannot silently become valid observations;
7. unrelated retrospective corrections are not applied;
8. current KRX/master data cannot resolve identities during this stage;
9. availability-restricted evidence cannot promote to Top30Observation;
10. it cannot create AssessmentPayload;
11. it cannot create a frozen assessment;
12. unresolved identities remain explicit;
13. deterministic parsed digest is stable;
14. source digest changes invalidate the derived representation;
15. parser version is bound to derived output;
16. JOB-0006 adversarial leakage protections still pass;
17. JOB-0007 write-once protections still pass;
18. JOB-0009 provenance safeguards still pass;
19. JOB-0010 provenance-repair tests still pass.

NO NETWORK REQUIREMENT

Do not require new Telegram network acquisition for this job.

Use the already repaired JOB-0010 provenance evidence and existing local raw
artifact.

Do not access .env or session contents unless absolutely necessary.
This job should normally require neither.

NO OUTCOME DATA

Do not access:

- future OHLCV;
- +5/+10/+20/+60 returns;
- future KRX identity;
- sector outcomes;
- success/failure labels.

DOCUMENTATION

Create:

docs/experiments/JOB-0011-real-pre-assessment-parsing.md

Document:

- real source used;
- provenance classification inherited from JOB-0010;
- parser adaptation;
- exact parsing result;
- source-name preservation;
- correction result;
- pre-assessment contract;
- quarantine mechanism;
- deterministic digest chain;
- why assessment promotion is currently blocked;
- limitations.

READINESS VERDICT

End with exactly one:

PREASSESSMENT_PIPELINE_READY
PREASSESSMENT_PIPELINE_READY_WITH_RESTRICTIONS
PARSER_REPAIR_REQUIRED
QUARANTINE_GATE_FAILED

The verdict applies only to moving to a policy review of historical
availability.

It does NOT authorize assessment creation, outcome joining, bulk Telegram
processing, or the full three-year study.

QUALITY

Run the complete pytest suite.
Run git diff --check.

Keep implementation minimal.

Do not commit or push.

FINAL RESPONSE

Report:

- requested model tier;
- actual model if telemetry exposes it;
- source message ID;
- inherited provenance classification;
- parsed row count;
- malformed/skipped rows;
- correction count;
- unresolved identity count;
- pre-assessment artifact path;
- source digest;
- parsed representation digest;
- quarantine gate result;
- tests;
- readiness verdict;
- residual risks;
- recommended next job.
